<%#
  Connect workspace layout.

  A deliberately reduced, full-screen shell for the Connect plugin. It keeps
  everything the application needs to stay functional (theme, CSRF token, CSP
  nonce, asset tags, tenant overrides, server notifications, flash messages)
  but drops the parts that would get in the way of a chat/calendar surface:

    * no navbar          - navigation happens through the icon rail
    * no footer          - vertical space is needed for the message list
    * no "main_content"  - the workspace is a top-level surface, not a fragment
      turbo frame          inside the regular application shell

  Because the plugin's app/views directory is appended to
  config.paths["app/views"] (see system/config/application.rb), this file is
  found by name alone - no extra registration is required.
%>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html data-theme="<%= CssHelper.theme(user: session[:user]) %>" lang="<%= session[:locale].present? ? session[:locale] : I18n.default_locale %>">
  <head>
    <title><%= [ @c[:header_title].presence, I18n.t("pl_connect.workspace.title"), SYSTEM[:server][:default][:system_title] ].compact.join(" - ") %></title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
    <meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
    <%= render_configurable_meta_tags(request: request) %>
    <%# The CSRF token is required by every fetch() call against
        PlConnectApiController: ApplicationController uses
        `protect_from_forgery with: :null_session` for JSON, so a request
        without the token silently loses its session and is answered with 401. %>
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>
    <%= yield :head %>
    <%= favicon_link_tag SYSTEM[:server][:default][:system_favicon] %>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag "application", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
    <%= javascript_include_tag "application", "data-turbo-track": "reload", type: "module" %>

    <%# Tenant-specific overrides, identical to the regular application layout. %>
    <% if session[:user]&.get_tenant %>
      <% tenant_name = session[:user].get_tenant[:name] %>
      <% css_path = Rails.root.join("public", "assets", "tenants", "tenant_#{tenant_name}.css") %>
      <% js_path  = Rails.root.join("public", "assets", "tenants", "tenant_#{tenant_name}.js") %>
      <%= stylesheet_link_tag "tenants/tenant_#{tenant_name}.css", media: "all" if css_path.exist? %>
      <%= javascript_include_tag "tenants/tenant_#{tenant_name}.js", nonce: request.content_security_policy_nonce if js_path.exist? %>
    <% end %>
  </head>

  <%#
    h-dvh instead of h-screen: on mobile browsers h-screen ignores the
    collapsing address bar, which would push the message composer out of view.
    overflow-hidden keeps the page itself from scrolling - only the individual
    panes scroll, which is what makes the surface feel like an application
    rather than a document.
  %>
  <body class="h-dvh overflow-hidden bg-base-200 text-base-content antialiased">
    <% if session[:user].present? %>
      <%# Server notifications are delivered through the same streams as in the
          regular layout, so system messages still reach the user while they
          are working inside the workspace. %>
      <%= turbo_stream_from "server_notification_#{session[:user][:id]}" %>
      <%= turbo_stream_from "server_notification" %>
      <span id="server_notification_div"></span>
      <span id="event_log_live_count" data-count="0" class="hidden"></span>
    <% end %>

    <%#
      Both workspace Stimulus controllers are mounted here rather than on the
      individual sections.

      pl-connect-chat needs the conversation list and the message pane (from
      the yielded section) as well as the search field in the top bar and the
      unread badge in the rail (from this layout). A Stimulus controller only
      sees targets inside its own element, so the wrapper that contains all
      four is the only correct mount point. Sections without a message pane run
      the same controller; it simply has nothing to render into.

      pl-connect-presence keeps the heartbeat alive across section changes and
      re-dispatches per-user notifications as DOM events, which is why it must
      not be bound to a single section either.

      pl-connect-call needs to be mounted here for the same reason as
      pl-connect-presence: an incoming call has to reach the user regardless of
      which section (or which conversation) they currently have open, and the
      call/video buttons it wires live inside the yielded message pane.

      pl-connect-user-picker is the shared "pick a colleague" modal used by the
      conversation sidebar's "+" button and the Calls surface's start-call
      buttons. It has to live here for the same reason: both triggers can be on
      screen regardless of which section is currently rendered.

      The i18n payloads hold static translations only - no user data and no
      configuration values - so embedding them into the page is safe.
      ice-servers-value is STUN/TURN connectivity configuration, not a secret
      by itself (see PlConnect::CallService.ice_servers) - a TURN credential
      configured there would need its own confidentiality handling, which is
      why that path is documented as GDPR-relevant at the source.
    %>
    <div class="flex h-full w-full"
         data-controller="pl-connect-chat pl-connect-presence pl-connect-call pl-connect-user-picker"
         data-pl-connect-chat-viewer-uuid-value="<%= @c[:pl_connect_user]&.uuid %>"
         data-pl-connect-chat-i18n-value="<%= pl_connect_chat_i18n.to_json %>"
         data-pl-connect-chat-initial-chat-uuid-value="<%= @c[:pl_connect_initial_chat_uuid] %>"
         data-pl-connect-presence-active-value="<%= @c[:pl_connect_presence_active] ? "true" : "false" %>"
         data-pl-connect-presence-i18n-value="<%= pl_connect_presence_i18n.to_json %>"
         data-pl-connect-call-active-value="<%= @c[:pl_connect_call_active] ? "true" : "false" %>"
         data-pl-connect-call-viewer-uuid-value="<%= @c[:pl_connect_user]&.uuid %>"
         data-pl-connect-call-i18n-value="<%= pl_connect_call_i18n.to_json %>"
         data-pl-connect-call-ice-servers-value="<%= PlConnect::CallService.ice_servers.to_json %>"
         data-pl-connect-call-pending-value="<%= @c[:pl_connect_pending_call] %>"
         data-pl-connect-user-picker-i18n-value="<%= pl_connect_user_picker_i18n.to_json %>">
      <%= render "pl_connect_workspace/rail" %>

      <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col">
        <%= render "pl_connect_workspace/topbar" %>

        <main class="flex min-h-0 flex-1">
          <%= yield %>
        </main>
      </div>

      <%# Incoming-call banner - shown regardless of which section/conversation
          is currently open, fed by the presence stream (PlConnectPresenceChannel
          "call.invite"), never by the chat stream. %>
      <div data-pl-connect-call-target="incomingBanner"
           class="hidden fixed inset-x-0 top-4 z-50 mx-auto w-full max-w-sm rounded-box bg-base-100 p-4 shadow-xl ring-1 ring-base-300">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <i class="fa-solid fa-phone-volume text-primary" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <p class="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate text-sm font-semibold" data-pl-connect-call-target="incomingLabel"></p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-3 flex justify-end gap-2">
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-error btn-sm" data-action="pl-connect-call#declineIncoming">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-phone-slash" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-success btn-sm" data-action="pl-connect-call#acceptIncoming">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-phone" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%# Active-call panel - local/remote video plus the mute/camera/screen/
          hangup controls. Positioned as a floating overlay rather than
          replacing the message pane, so the conversation stays usable (e.g. to
          keep typing) while a call is running. %>
      <div data-pl-connect-call-target="activePanel"
           class="hidden fixed inset-x-4 bottom-4 z-40 flex flex-col gap-2 rounded-box bg-base-100 p-3 shadow-xl ring-1 ring-base-300 sm:inset-x-auto sm:right-4 sm:w-[28rem]">
        <p class="truncate text-sm font-semibold" data-pl-connect-call-target="statusLabel"></p>
        <div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-box bg-black">
          <%# One <video> per remote participant is appended here at runtime by
              pl_connect_call_controller.js (see _getOrCreateRemoteVideo) - a
              1:1 call simply ends up with a single tile. %>
          <div data-pl-connect-call-target="remoteVideos" class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-1 empty:grid-cols-1"></div>
          <video data-pl-connect-call-target="localVideo" class="absolute bottom-2 right-2 h-16 w-24 rounded border border-base-100 bg-black" autoplay playsinline muted></video>
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-center gap-2">
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-circle btn-sm" data-action="pl-connect-call#toggleAudio" data-pl-connect-call-target="audioButton">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-microphone" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-circle btn-sm" data-action="pl-connect-call#toggleVideo" data-pl-connect-call-target="videoButton">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-video" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-circle btn-sm" data-action="pl-connect-call#toggleScreen" data-pl-connect-call-target="screenButton">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-display" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-circle btn-sm btn-error" data-action="pl-connect-call#hangup">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-phone-slash" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%#
        Shared "pick a colleague" modal used by both the conversation sidebar's
        "+" button (mode "chat") and the Calls surface's start-call buttons
        (mode "call"). Picking a user resolves/creates the 1:1 chat through
        /pl_connect_api/open_direct and navigates to it (see
        pl_connect_user_picker_controller.js) - no in-place list refresh, so
        the server-rendered sidebar and the new-conversation flow cannot drift
        apart in what counts as "the current conversation list".
      %>
      <div data-pl-connect-user-picker-target="overlay"
           class="hidden fixed inset-0 z-50 flex items-start justify-center bg-black/40 pt-24"
           data-action="click->pl-connect-user-picker#closeOnBackdrop keydown->pl-connect-user-picker#onKeydown">
        <div class="w-full max-w-sm rounded-box bg-base-100 p-4 shadow-xl ring-1 ring-base-300">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
            <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold"><%= I18n.t("pl_connect.user_picker.title") %></h2>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-xs" data-action="pl-connect-user-picker#close">
              <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </button>
          </div>

          <input type="text"
                 class="input input-bordered input-sm mt-3 w-full"
                 placeholder="<%= I18n.t("pl_connect.user_picker.search_placeholder") %>"
                 autocomplete="off"
                 data-pl-connect-user-picker-target="input"
                 data-action="input->pl-connect-user-picker#onInput">

          <p data-pl-connect-user-picker-target="error" class="hidden mt-2 text-xs text-error"></p>

          <div data-pl-connect-user-picker-target="results" class="mt-2 max-h-64 overflow-y-auto"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%= render partial: "common/fragment_alerts" %>
  </body>
</html>
